.TH TENSOR 2
.SH NAME
tensor \- a convolutional network's arithmetic, natively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "tensor.m";
tensor := load Tensor Tensor->PATH;

None, Relu, Sigmoid, Silu: con iota;

conv:      fn(in: array of byte, c, h, w: int,
               wt: array of byte, oc, kh, kw, stride, pad, group: int,
               bias: array of byte, act: int, out: array of byte);
add:       fn(a, b, out: array of byte);
act:       fn(in, out: array of byte, act: int);
maxpool:   fn(in: array of byte, c, h, w, k, stride, pad: int, out: array of byte);
up2:       fn(in: array of byte, c, h, w: int, out: array of byte);
s2d:       fn(in: array of byte, c, h, w: int, out: array of byte);
letterbox: fn(pix: array of byte, w, h: int, scale: real,
               fill, bgr: int, out: array of byte, ow, oh: int);
toreal:    fn(t: array of byte, out: array of real);
fromreal:  fn(r: array of real, out: array of byte);
kind:      fn(): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B $Tensor
is built in, as
.B $I420
is: the arithmetic a network spends its time in, done natively, so a
model can be run by a Limbo program
.RB ( /dis/lib/visnet.dis ,
for
.IR visionfs (4))
that decides everything else.
It keeps nothing between calls.
.PP
A tensor is an array of byte holding 32-bit floats, little-endian:
.I c
planes of
.I h
rows of
.IR w ,
4-byte aligned (an array, or a slice of one at a multiple of 4).
.PP
.I Conv
computes
.I out
.RI ( oc
by
.I oh
by
.IR ow ,
.I oh
being
.RI ( h +2 pad - kh )/ stride +1
and
.I ow
likewise) as the activation of the convolution of
.I in
by
.I wt
.RI ( oc
by
.IR c / group
by
.I kh
by
.IR kw )
plus
.I bias
.RI ( oc );
.I group
is 1 or
.I c
(a depthwise convolution, with
.I oc
=
.IR c ).
.I Add
adds two tensors of one length,
.I act
applies an activation,
.I maxpool
takes maxima over
.I k
by
.I k
(padded with minus infinity),
.I up2
doubles the rows and columns (nearest), and
.I s2d
moves each 2 by 2 cell's samples (0,0) (1,0) (0,1) (1,1) to four times
the channels.
.PP
.I Letterbox
makes a network's input, 3 by
.I oh
by
.IR ow ,
from a picture of
.I w
by
.I h
.B Draw->RGB24
pixels (blue, green, red in memory): scaled by
.I scale
with bilinear interpolation into the top left corner, the rest
.IR fill ,
its channels red, green, blue, or blue, green, red if
.IR bgr .
.I Toreal
and
.I fromreal
convert between a tensor and an array of real of as many elements.
.I Kind
says what the arithmetic was compiled as:
.B neon
on arm64,
.B c
elsewhere.
.PP
Each function checks every size against its arrays before it begins,
raising
.B "array bounds error"
for any that does not fit, so none reads or writes outside them; and
lets the VM's other programs run while it computes.
.SH SOURCE
.B /libinterp/tensor.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR visionfs (4)
.SH BUGS
32-bit floats only: on a Cortex-A72 8-bit arithmetic without a dot
product instruction is slower.
